\section{Release Checklist}

The release process has three stages. Each stage has its own
verification steps, and the operator records the result in the run book
before the next stage starts.

\begin{enumerate}
\item Prepare the build host.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Clear the previous build directory.
  \item Confirm that the toolchain version matches the manifest.
  \end{itemize}
\item Compile and install the artifacts.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Run the release target.
  \item Copy the install tree to the staging share.
\item Run the acceptance suite.
\end{enumerate}

After the third stage the operator signs the run book and closes the
ticket. A failure at any stage returns the release to stage one.

