\section{Relative Cost}

The table gives the measured cost of each stage against the cost of the
whole pipeline. The ratios are exact, so we print them as fractions and
not as decimals.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
Stage & Value & Ratio \\
Fetch   & 12 & $\frac{1}{4}$ \\
Decode  & 40 & $\frac{2}{5}$ \\
Execute & 18 & \frac{3}{8} \\
Retire  &  6 & $\frac{1}{8}$ \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The fetch stage dominates on the small model. On the large model the
execute stage takes more than half of the total, so the ratios in the
table apply to the small model only.

