\section{Scaled Attention}

The attention weights are a softmax over the scaled products of the
query and the key vectors. The scale keeps the products small when the
head dimension grows.

\begin{displaymath}
s_{ij} = \frac{q_i \cdot k_j}
\end{displaymath}

The denominator is the square root of the head dimension $d$, not of
the model dimension. For a model dimension of 512 and eight heads the
head dimension is 64, so the scale is 8.

The softmax then runs over the index $j$ for each fixed $i$. The result
is a row of weights that sums to one.

\section{Scaled Attention}

The attention weights are a softmax over the scaled products of the
query and the key vectors. The scale keeps the products small when the
head dimension grows.

\begin{displaymath}
s_{ij} = \frac{q_i \cdot k_j}{\sqrt{d}}
\end{displaymath}

The denominator is the square root of the head dimension $d$, not of
the model dimension. For a model dimension of 512 and eight heads the
head dimension is 64, so the scale is 8.

The softmax then runs over the index $j$ for each fixed $i$. The result
is a row of weights that sums to one.

