\section{Symbols}

The macros below keep the notation consistent through the chapter. Each
macro takes one argument.

\newcommand{\gradient}[1]{\nabla #1}
\newcommand{\vec}[1]{\mathbf{#1}}
\newcommand{\norm}[1]{\| #1 \|}

The weight vector is $\vec{w}$ and its gradient is $\gradient{L}$. The
step size is chosen so that $\vec{w}$ moves by a fixed amount at each
update.

We write the length of the step as $\norm{\vec{w}}$, and we clip the
step when the length is larger than the threshold. The threshold is a
constant for the whole run.

